<input_format>
A test case set consists of an abstract step sequence and a parameter combinations table.

Step structure:
```
{TestCaseSetName}
    {Step Name}    step_type:flow
    {Step Name}    param=${placeholder}    step_type:check
```
- `step_type:flow` = action step; `step_type:check` = validation step
- `${placeholder}` is resolved in the parameter table — treat as abstract.
</input_format>

<test_case_set>
```
{{ agent.step_sequence }}
```
</test_case_set>

<parameter_combinations>
```
{{ agent.parameter_combinations }}
```
</parameter_combinations>

<task>
Write exactly one sentence that describes the test objective of this test case set.
The sentence must start with "This test case set verifies..." and capture the overall purpose of the abstract test sequence.
Do not add preconditions, expected results, or domain details that are not explicit in the artifact.
</task>

<output_format>
Plain text, one sentence only:
```
This test case set verifies [objective].
```
- No leading whitespace or blank lines.
- Do not alter any identifiers from the input.
</output_format>